<!--
  Results: every component kind a Result Organizer has been seen to carry, in
  one matched organizer, so the shared-context guard is pinned against vendor
  shapes and not just the IG-conformant ones (#1504).

  Hand-authored. The **shapes** (element kinds, templateIds, what is present or
  absent) are modelled on Epic eICR output; every value is fabricated, and ids
  use the HL7 example OID 2.16.840.1.113883.19.5.

  Organizer 1 (matched via 94500-6) carries, in order:
    - a specimen collection <procedure> with **no** templateId      -> context, kept
    - the matched Result Observation                                -> kept
    - an unmatched Result Observation                               -> pruned
    - an Epic proprietary result <observation> (...72.3.4)          -> pruned ("16" rows)
    - an Epic <procedure> (...72.3.7), nullFlavored code            -> context, kept
    - a Specimen Collection Procedure mis-sent as an
      <observation> carrying ...4.415                               -> context, kept
    - a Comment Activity <act> (...4.64)                            -> context, kept
    - a Laboratory Result Status <observation> (...4.418)           -> context, kept
    - a nested <organizer> whose only result is unmatched           -> pruned

  Organizer 2 matches nothing, so it is removed whole and its templateId-less
  specimen procedure goes with it: the carve-out only fires inside a matched
  entry.
-->
